<!--
  T-Motor (LIGPOWER) 13x4.4 CF propeller, the one the MN3510 datasheet tests with. The static point is the
  datasheet's own: on the KV630 at 14.8 V it gives 540 g at 4500 rpm through 1500 g at 7300 rpm, which is
  C_T 0.065-0.069 and C_P 0.021-0.023 at every throttle once the motor's copper and idle losses are taken off
  the electrical watts (RobotShop copy of the datasheet, ligpower_mn3510_kv630_high_performance_uav_motor_f).
  No wind tunnel has measured this blade, so the fall-off with advance ratio is the shape of the nearest measured
  13-inch APC electric, the 13x6.5 in UIUC's propeller database volume 4 (static run 0537od at 5953 rpm, dynamic
  run 0543od at 5967 rpm, a straight line past its last point to zero thrust), scaled to the datasheet's static
  level and compressed in J by the pitch ratio 4.4/6.5, since a flatter blade runs out of thrust sooner.

  The mesh is the source model's 13.62-inch blade; the numbers are the 13-inch prop's. Inertia is a 14 g
  carbon blade as a rod: m L^2 / 12.
-->
